Author:     Stephen A Pohl <spohl@mozilla.com>
AuthorDate: Wed Aug 5 19:18:51 2026 +0000
Commit:     spohl@mozilla.com <spohl@mozilla.com>
CommitDate: Wed Aug 5 19:20:58 2026 +0000

    Bug 2052415: Count unread mail across every account's inbox for the macOS badge, not just already-loaded folders. r=arschmitz,edicharry

    MailNotificationService computes the dock badge total by iterating nsIMsgFolder.descendants over each account's root folder. descendants only returns subfolders that have already been discovered into memory. At startup the subfolders of accounts other than the one currently shown in the folder pane have not been discovered yet, so their inboxes are skipped, and the counts later load from the folder cache without firing a TotalUnreadMessages change notification that would correct the running total. The result is a permanent, deterministic under-count (typically zero when no account's inbox happens to be loaded) for people with more than one account, which on macOS shows up as a missing dock badge even though unread mail is visible in the folder pane.

    Fix this at the source in nsMsgDBFolder::GetDescendants by forcing the message store to discover the folder's children before enumerating them. This is protocol-agnostic (it goes through nsIMsgPluggableStore) and runs at most once per folder. Because the under-count is fixed in descendants itself, every caller that walks descendants sees the complete hierarchy, not just the notification service. Panorama keeps the hierarchy in its own folder database, so it is left alone.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310235

diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBFolder.cpp b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBFolder.cpp
index ed8bffe3b4a..859dbae826f 100644
--- a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBFolder.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBFolder.cpp
@@ -239,6 +239,7 @@ nsMsgDBFolder::nsMsgDBFolder(void)
       mNotifyCountChanges(true),
       mExpungedBytes(0),
       mInitializedFromCache(false),
+      mDiscoveredSubFolders(false),
       mSemaphoreHolder(nullptr),
       mNumPendingUnreadMessages(0),
       mNumPendingTotalMessages(0),
@@ -4962,6 +4963,40 @@ NS_IMETHODIMP nsMsgDBFolder::GetMessageHeader(nsMsgKey msgKey,
 NS_IMETHODIMP nsMsgDBFolder::GetDescendants(
     nsTArray<RefPtr<nsIMsgFolder>>& aDescendants) {
   aDescendants.Clear();
+
+  // `mSubFolders` only holds folders that have already been discovered into
+  // memory. At startup the subfolders of accounts other than the one shown in
+  // the folder pane have not been discovered yet, so callers that walk the
+  // descendants (for example the unread-count badge) would miss them. Ask the
+  // message store which children exist on disk and add any that are missing,
+  // so descendant enumeration is complete regardless of what has been loaded
+  // so far. The recursion below walks into each child, which discovers deeper
+  // levels in turn. Panorama keeps the hierarchy in its folder database rather
+  // than the store, so it does not need this.
+  if (!mDiscoveredSubFolders &&
+      !StaticPrefs::mail_panorama_enabled_AtStartup()) {
+    // Set the flag before discovering to guard against re-entrancy while the
+    // store adds the subfolders.
+    mDiscoveredSubFolders = true;
+    nsCOMPtr<nsIMsgPluggableStore> store;
+    if (NS_SUCCEEDED(GetMsgStore(getter_AddRefs(store))) && store) {
+      // Use DiscoverChildFolders (a read-only listing) rather than
+      // DiscoverSubFolders, which as a side effect creates a directory at the
+      // folder path when it does not exist yet and would corrupt folders whose
+      // store file has not been written.
+      nsTArray<nsCString> childNames;
+      if (NS_SUCCEEDED(store->DiscoverChildFolders(this, childNames))) {
+        for (const auto& childName : childNames) {
+          nsCOMPtr<nsIMsgFolder> child;
+          GetChildNamed(childName, getter_AddRefs(child));
+          if (!child) {
+            AddSubfolder(childName, getter_AddRefs(child));
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   for (nsIMsgFolder* child : mSubFolders) {
     aDescendants.AppendElement(child);
     nsTArray<RefPtr<nsIMsgFolder>> grandchildren;
